{
  "provenance": "TradingView measurements, 2026-11-02. Each sha256 is the SHA-256 of that probe's TradingView export: the trades list or the reply that stops the run. Each source_sha256 identifies the measured source, not necessarily the repository fixture. The export files are not stored in the repository. For float_counter_*, first_end_read_*, int_counter_float_end and step_reads_counter_descending, fixtures preserve the measured expressions but may change strategy titles, comments and whitespace; float_counter_helper_value also places the helper body on its declaration line. The float-counter value and thirteen older iteration-count rows were measured on BINANCE:BTCUSDT 60, including seven tolerance-bracket probes at 12:22; each quantity holds on all 205 entries. The four additional large/small-step rows preserve every source byte except the strategy title; counts 3, 4, 3 and 3 are encoded as entry quantities 1.03, 1.04, 1.03 and 1.03 on all 180 exported entries. Their trade schedule is every eight bars from bar 0, with a close on the next bar. The first_end_read_start_two_down and first_end_read_start_two_up probes were measured at 11:57 on BINANCE:BTCUSDT 60; their exports have identical bytes and all 205 entries have quantity 1.1. The zero-entry probe is recorded separately because its accumulator starts at 0. The fstep_* sources are exact copies of the accepted TradingView scripts; their entry quantities encode 5, 7 and 3 loop iterations as 1 + count / 100. Their trade schedule is every eight bars from bar 0, with a close on the next bar. Compile-refusal spans use TradingView's 1-based inclusive end columns.",
  "division_provenance": "The division_start_no_step, division_start_int_step, division_named_start, division_end_only and division_counter_value fixtures copy the measured v01 through v05 scripts byte for byte. fractional_input and fractional_series copy the measured fractional-input.pine and fractional-series.pine byte for byte. All seven exports contain 205 entries. The v01 and v03 exports are the same file. The series export alternates odd n (10.5, 103 entries) and even n (12, 102 entries), starting with odd n. Each sha256 below is the supplied full TradingView export digest; the source hashes identify the copied scripts. Carrier controls derive their 10.5 oracle from fractional_input's identical loop shape; they do not claim separate TradingView tapes.",
  "fractional_consumer_provenance": "TradingView accepted descending.pine, array-index.pine and counter-string.pine on 2026-11-02 at 22:59. fractional_descending.pine, fractional_array_index.pine and counter_string.pine copy those sources byte for byte. The descending export has 205 entries of quantity 4.5. The array-index export has 205 entries of quantity 120: indices 2.5, 3.5 and 4.5 truncate to 2, 3 and 4. The counter-string export has 615 entries of quantity 1, with 205 entries for each exact id recorded below. Full export and source digests are the supplied measurement receipts. The counter_tostring known gap records current engine text separately from TradingView's 18-place ids.",
